  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Nafees vs State Of U.P. on 5 May, 2025 Author: Ashutosh Srivastava Bench: Ashutosh Srivastava High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2025:Ahc:71627 Court No. - 68 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 4952 of 2025 Applicant :- Nafees",
    "facts": "This bail application under Section 483 of Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 has been moved on behalf of accused-applicant seeking enlargement on bail in Case Crime No. 473 of 2024, under 274, 275 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 and Sections 26(2), (i) (iv) & 59(i) of the Food Safety & Standard Act, 2006, Police Station Khurja Dehat, District Bulandshahar.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant argued that the accused-applicant is innocent and he has been falsely implicated in this very case crime number. Learned counsel for the applicant submits that applicant dos not directly manufacture the alleged diary products, but purchases them from the market. Learned counsel for the applicant submits that the maximum punishment in the aforesaid sections are punishable with six months and the applicant has already undergone period of about five months. It is further submitted that on the similar footing the co-accused Firoz Khan has been granted bail by this Court vide order dated 09.04.2025 passed in Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. 8248 of 2025, therefore, applicant is also entitled to be released on bail. The applicant is languishing in jail since 05.12.2024. He has no criminal antecedent and there is no likelihood of his fleeing from course of justice or tampering with evidence in case of release on bail. Hence, bail has been prayed for. Learned AGA has vehemently opposed the prayer for bail.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant argued that the accused-applicant is innocent and he has been falsely implicated in this very case crime number. Learned counsel for the applicant submits that applicant dos not directly manufacture the alleged diary products, but purchases them from the market.",
    "respondent_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant submits that the maximum punishment in the aforesaid sections are punishable with six months and the applicant has already undergone period of about five months. It is further submitted that on the similar footing the co-accused Firoz Khan has been granted bail by this Court vide order dated 09.04.2025 passed in Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. 8248 of 2025, therefore, applicant is also entitled to be released on bail. The applicant is languishing in jail since 05.12.2024. He has no criminal antecedent and there is no likelihood of his fleeing from course of justice or tampering with evidence in case of release on bail. Hence, bail has been prayed for. Learned AGA has vehemently opposed the prayer for bail.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
